{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791537818,"nonce":"LDc59e72NzP8g4fzN6vbJUD8KOw=","title":"Native window waits can block interpreter fibers indefinitely: after a window starts waiting, a Haxe worker parked in Sys.sleep cannot reach its due timer without another UI event. Reproduced by Ashui IdleWake in interp; hybrid compiled workers passed. Related to, but distinct from, issue 4855ac5 (pending Future.await after opening AppKit).","message":"Fixed in 1f27156: ash_host_wait joins the current scheduler to a native host wait, running ready work and shortening the timeout to the next fiber deadline. Endpoint completions notify the host through a thread-safe wake operation latched by xwindow. ash_host_resumed clears the registration; callback code must remain loaded for process lifetime. Runtime dispatch v8 includes both hooks so alternate schedulers can implement the contract. hlwindow 4bacd76 resolves hooks optionally; old Ash retains bounded waits.\n\nVerified 2 host-wait unit tests and 3 runtime-table tests; Ashui IdleWake passes interp and hybrid with worker signal, deferred timer, redraw and quit. Existing native-window Future.await issue 4855ac5 remains open; this does not claim to resolve that separate reproducer.","files":null}]}